eer, nor a dozen of vvine, ſince he paid his garniſh—the gentlemen get drunk vvith nothing but your damned religion.— […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bar","barroom"],"antonyms":["humming"],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, abbreviation, alt-of, broadly, ellipsis","register":"UK, abbreviation, alt-of, broadly, ellipsis","wordFamily":["ascitic tap","bubble tap","center tap","champagne tap","cold tap","hot tap","lifetap","mixer tap","on tap","on the tap","pericardial tap","pleural tap","plug tap","power tap","relocatable power tap","spinal tap","stop-tap","tap bolt","tap changer","tap cinder","tap drill","taphole","taphouse","taplash","tapless","tapman","tappee","taproom","taproot","tapware"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:90d3ba6cf96e01fa9d","definition":"A connection made to an electrical or fluid conductor without breaking it; a tapping.","example":"The system was barely keeping pressure due to all of the ill-advised taps along its length.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["clap","knock","pat","ping","plip","plonk","plop","rap","slam","slap","smack","spank","tap"],"antonyms":["humming"],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, broadly","register":"UK, broadly","wordFamily":["ascitic tap","bubble tap","center tap","champagne tap","cold tap","hot tap","lifetap","mixer tap","on tap","on the tap","pericardial tap","pleural tap","plug tap","power tap","relocatable power tap","spinal tap","stop-tap","tap bolt","tap changer","tap cinder","tap drill","taphole","taphouse","taplash","tapless","tapman","tappee","taproom","taproot","tapware"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:68d419ea670915ea79","definition":"To furnish (a container, etc.) with a tap (noun etymology 1, noun sense 2.2) so that liquid can be drawn.","example":"There's a very pretty brew in tap at The Pure Drop—though, to be sure, not so good as at Rolliver's.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly, transitive","wordFamily":["ascitic tap","bubble tap","center tap","champagne tap","cold tap","hot tap","lifetap","mixer tap","on tap","on the tap","pericardial tap","pleural tap","plug tap","power tap","relocatable power tap","spinal tap","stop-tap","tap bolt","tap changer","tap cinder","tap drill","taphole","taphouse","taplash","tapless","tapman","tappee","taproom","taproot","tapware"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fb47b4c78b8f9839cf","definition":"To draw off (a liquid) from a container or other source; also, to draw off a liquid from (a container or other source).","example":"He tapped the ten-year-old whiskey from its barrel.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["ascitic tap","bubble tap","center tap","champagne tap","cold tap","hot tap","lifetap","mixer tap","on tap","on the tap","pericardial tap","pleural tap","plug tap","power tap","relocatable power tap","spinal tap","stop-tap","tap bolt","tap changer","tap cinder","tap drill","taphole","taphouse","taplash","tapless","tapman","tappee","taproom","taproot","tapware"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:68f24b6f664c5afd81","definition":"To break into or open up (a thing) so as to obtain something; to exploit, to penetrate; tap into.","example":"Businesses are trying to tap the youth market.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["ascitic tap","bubble tap","center tap","champagne tap","cold tap","hot tap","lifetap","mixer tap","on tap","on the tap","pericardial tap","pleural tap","plug tap","power tap","relocatable power tap","spinal tap","stop-tap","tap bolt","tap changer","tap cinder","tap drill","taphole","taphouse","taplash","tapless","tapman","tappee","taproom","taproot","tapware"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e63c326215c1f0708","definition":"To deplete (something); to tap out.","example":"At the range of a couple of hundred yards we emptied our magazines, firing bullet after bullet into the beasts, but with no more effect than if we were pelting them with pellets of paper. Their slow reptilian natures cared nothing for wounds, and the springs of their lives, with no special brain centre but scattered throughout their spinal cords, could not be tapped by any modern weapons.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["ascitic tap","bubble tap","center tap","champagne tap","cold tap","hot tap","lifetap","mixer tap","on tap","on the tap","pericardial tap","pleural tap","plug tap","power tap","relocatable power tap","spinal tap","stop-tap","tap bolt","tap changer","tap cinder","tap drill","taphole","taphouse","taplash","tapless","tapman","tappee","taproom","taproot","tapware"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tap#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:90fc6c584490b59306","definition":"To ask or beg for (something) to be given for free; to cadge, to scrounge; also, to ask or beg (someone) to give something for free.","example":"I tried to tap a cigarette off him, but he wouldn’t give me one.","pos":"verb","s